KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp14
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ generic lambda: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body
--
N5008 [expr.prim.lambda.closure]/4, [temp.inst]/11: the function call
operator of a generic lambda is a member function template, instantiated
only for the argument types it is called with (auto = double here).  The
front end also type-checks the body with `signed int' for auto: it
instantiates fmt<int>, whose call h(int) is ambiguous, and drops that body
("C++ front-end dropped the body of function 'fmt<signed_int>'").  The
verdict is unaffected here.  In libstdc++ 13's <format> the same happens to
_Formatting_scanner::_M_format_arg's visitor (`using _Type =
remove_reference_t<decltype(__arg)>;'): __formatter_fp::format is
instantiated with an unresolved _Type and dropped (format:1422;
cpp11_namespace_reopened_after_qualified_member_template_definition/
test_libstdcxx.desc).  Pre-existing (bin53).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept
this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
